ns. I came for lunch and it wasn't too packed, didn't have to wait for a table. They had live jazz music playing and the vibe the band have off was so fun and the restaurant was so into it. The music was great. It was pretty loud, so if you have kids or want a quiet meal, ask for a seat in the back. The food was delicious. The BBQ sauce is so good. We all tried something different and we're all very satisfied with our choices."},{"business_id":"TVDe34aKHkjaEOtCqffwbw","review_id":"-3SHVRMfGN55932Zzbupwg","date":"2020-04-06T17:01:21","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.931746244430542,"text_excerpt":"What a lively place! We stopped in for beers and happy hour treats (instead of usual beignets). There was a $5 cover charge here and it was well worth it! We all got a round of beers and some appetizers from the menu. The boudain was really tasty but the catfish bites were the main hit! The music was great and people were dancing and living it up in here! They were really good about interacting with the audience."},{"business_id":"TVDe34aKHkjaEOtCqffwbw","review_id":"eqO5vy-TlDNwjo__5G8X2A","date":"2017-03-31T18:19:58","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.92951899766922,"text_excerpt":"My friend and I came over to this place ON St. Patrick's day, after the parade (or close to the end of it). There was a $5 charge to come in because they didn't want to make the restroom available to just anybody. I have to admit, this was very smart on their part because they took advantage of a great opportunity. The restrooms were very well worth the $5 charge, because we then ended up staying for the jazz AND the food. The band that was playing, was awesome! We listened to some R-E-S-P-E-C-T and some Otis Redding...it was really good! For starters, I ordered a cup of the Gumbo Ya Ya - which was fantastic! The menu detailed it as \"a New Orleans classic chicken and Andouille sausage sim..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"TVDe34aKHkjaEOtCqffwbw","photo_id":"yG4aB5NHkZ6wu-p8d20Lng","label